 Gingerich]] proposed that lemuriform primates evolved from one of several genera of European adapids based on similarities between the front lower teeth of adapids and the [[toothcomb]] of extant lemuriforms; however, this view is not strongly supported due to a lack of clear transitional fossils.{{Sfn|Rose|2006|p=182 & 186}}  Instead, lemuriforms may be descended from a very early branch of Asian cercamoniines or sivaladapids that immigrated to northern Africa.{{Sfn|Godinot|2006|p=446}}{{Sfn|Tabuce|Marivaux|Lebrun|Adaci|2009|pp=4091–4092}}

