blocks.ctx:
ylogenetics]].  They have been assigned a new subfamily status, [[Deomyinae]].

Molecular phylogenetic studies of Murinae include Lecompte, et al. (2008),{{sfn|Lecompte|Aplin|Denys|Catzeflis|2008}} which analyzes African murine species based on the mitochondrial [[cytochrome b]] gene and two nuclear gene fragments. Lecompte, et al. (2008) estimates that African murines colonized Africa from Asia approximately 11 million years ago during the [[Miocene]].

The following [[phylogeny]] of 16 Murinae [[genus|genera]], based on [[molecular phylogenetic]] analysis of the [[RBP3|Interphotoreceptor Retinoid Binding Protein]] (IRBP) gene, is from Jansa & Weksler (2004: 264).{{sfn|Jansa|Weksler|2004}}

