The following cladogram is from a phylogenetic analysis by Peyre de Fabrègues ''et al.'', 2020. Here, Riojasauridae was placed in a more derived position, lying closer to [[Sauropoda]] than to [[Massospondylidae]], and appearing as the [[out group]] to the clade formed by the genus ''Seitaad'' and the Sauropodiformes.<ref name="Fabrègues2020" /> The Massospondylidae and the taxa considered to be related to the family by Yates, are shown to be represent more primitive lineages.<ref name = "Fabrègues2020" />

