h von Reumont ''et al.'' (2012) results.{{r|Oakley2013|von Reumont2012}}

New proposed by Oakley ''et al.'' clades are:
*Hexanauplia (refers to six ("hexa-") [[Crustacean larvae#Nauplius|naupliar]] [[moulting|molts]])—[[Copepod|Copepoda]], [[Thecostraca]].
*Allotriocarida ("allotrios" is "strange", "carida" is "shrimp")—[[Cephalocarida]], [[Branchiopoda]], [[Remipedia]], [[Hexapoda]].{{r|Oakley2013}}

Note: the Allotriocarida clade was also recovered in 2005 by Regier ''et al.'' as Clade #33,{{r|Regier2005}} but relations within it were different, and they did not choose a name for it.

