blocks.ctx:
nce vertebrates. Because the [[fossil]] record of early chordates is poor, only [[molecular phylogenetics]] offers a reasonable prospect of dating their emergence. However, the use of molecular [[phylogenetics]] for dating evolutionary transitions is controversial. It has proven difficult to produce a detailed classification within the living chordates. Attempts to produce evolutionary "[[phylogenetic tree|family trees]]" show that many of the traditional [[class (biology)|classes]] are [[paraphyletic]].{{citation needed|date=December 2024}}

